      body: 'Here is a made-up story to hold the idea. In a town in Peru a boy named Mateo was getting ready for a long bus trip with his father. His older cousin, who liked to tease, told him that his father had packed no food at all and that they would go hungry for two days. Mateo did not ask his father. He believed his cousin. That night he took rolls from the kitchen and hid them in his pillowcase, in his shoes, and in the pocket of his coat. In the morning his father found crumbs all the way down the hall and a boy who would not look at him. He did not shout. He opened the big bag by the door and showed Mateo the bread, the cheese, the oranges and the sweets packed for the two of them. Mateo had taken what he was told not to take, and that was wrong. But it began the moment he believed his father would not look after him. "Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding." (Proverbs 3:5)',
